        "title": "fix(nvidia): sync recommended models with featured catalog",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nKeeps OpenClaw's recommended NVIDIA Endpoint models aligned exactly with NVIDIA's authoritative featured-model catalog instead of leaving users with stale recommendations. The bundled fallback and provider documentation contain only NVIDIA's current five featured models, while authenticated setup and model-selection paths continue pulling the live catalog from NVIDIA's static JSON feed.\n\n### What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where NVIDIA Endpoint users could see outdated recommended models and metadata after NVIDIA updated its featured catalog.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Refresh the bundled NVIDIA fallback with Nemotron 3 Ultra, Nemotron 3 Super, GLM 5.2, Kimi K2.6, and Minimax M3 using the values from NVIDIA's featured-model JSON.\n- Remove every bundled model row that is absent from NVIDIA's current feed.\n- Match feed-provided names, context windows, and max-output values exactly; normalize only Super's bare model ID through the existing NVIDIA prefix rule.\n- Update the NVIDIA provider documentation to match the authoritative catalog.\n- Extend NVIDIA catalog, onboarding, and registration tests for the refreshed rows.\n\n### Why This Change Was Made\n\nNVIDIA's public `featured-models.json` is the source of truth for current recommendations. OpenClaw already fetches that feed for authenticated setup and model selection; this change also aligns the bundled unavailable-feed fallback and documentation with the same source.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Evidence\n\n- Live equality check against `https://assets.ngc.nvidia.com/products/api-catalog/featured-models.json` passed for all five expected rows and their context/max-output metadata.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/nvidia/provider-catalog.test.ts extensions/nvidia/index.test.ts extensions/nvidia/onboard.test.ts` — 26 tests passed.\n- `corepack pnpm docs:check-mdx` — passed.\n- `corepack pnpm docs:check-links` — 5,544 internal links checked, 0 broken.\n- `corepack pnpm format:docs:check` — passed.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` — passed.\n\n## Notes\n\n### User Impact\n\nNew NVIDIA setup and model-selection flows show the current featured models from NVIDIA's live catalog. If that feed is unavailable, the bundled fallback presents exactly the same five models. Previously bundled model refs that are no longer present in NVIDIA's feed are intentionally removed rather than retained as compatibility-only rows.\n\nRelated: https://github.com/NVIDIA-dev/openclaw-tracking/issues/817\n",
